column.value:
You are a data security expert. Analyze this database schema and suggest masking policies.
Schema Information: {schemaInfo}
User Context: {userContext}
Respond with ONLY valid JSON array of suggestions: [ { "tableName": "users", "fieldName": "email", "dataType": "VARCHAR", "suggestedStrategy": "partial", "confidence": 0.9, "reason": "Email field detected - contains PII", "sampleValue": "j***@example.com", "detectionMethod": "field_name", "maskingPattern": "***", "preserveChars": 4, "maskChar": "*", "sensitivityLevel": "MEDIUM" } ]
Detection Rules: 1. Field names containing: email, mail -> EMAIL masking 2. Field names containing: ssn, social -> SSN masking (full or last 4) 3. Field names containing: credit, card, cc -> Credit card masking 4. Field names containing: name, fname, lname -> Name masking 5. Field names containing: phone, mobile -> Phone masking 6. Field names containing: password, pass -> Full masking/hashing 7. Field names containing: address -> Address masking 8. Date fields with birth, dob -> Date masking 9. Field names containing: pan, pan_number, pan_no -> Indian PAN (Permanent Account Number) masking - partial, preserve last 4 10. Field names containing: aadhaar, aadhar, aadhaar_number, aadhar_number -> Indian Aadhaar number masking - partial, preserve last 4
Sensitivity Levels: - LOW: Basic contact info - MEDIUM: Email, phone, address - HIGH: SSN, PAN, Aadhaar, financial data - CRITICAL: Passwords, keys
